    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d38-a2">

                <pb facs="0426" n="416" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv05/pg416"/>

                <head>Appendix II to IC–179B</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-05-01"><hi rendition="#small-caps">May</hi> 1,
                        1919</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#center">[<hi rendition="#italic">Note From the Secretary General of
                        the Conference</hi>]</p>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Note</hi>:</p>
                <p>Guided by the preamble of the Treaty providing the “resumption of official
                    relations” with Germany, the Drafting Committee have been of opinion that <list>
                        <item>Bolivia</item>
                        <item>Ecuador</item>
                        <item>Peru</item>
                        <item>Uruguay</item>
                    </list></p>
                <p rendition="#flush">should be included in the Allied and Associated Powers which
                    are to resume those relations.</p>
                <p>The above mentioned Powers, as is well known, did not declare war upon Germany
                    but merely severed diplomatic relations with her. It will be noticed, however,
                    that Uruguay has performed acts of war (Germany ships).</p>
                <pb facs="0427" n="417" xml:id="pg417"/>
                <p>According to Article I of the Regulations those Powers have been admitted to the
                    work of the Conference and have since the beginning taken a part in it.</p>
                <p>If the view of the Drafting Committee is correct it will be expedient: <list>
                        <label>1.</label>
                        <item>—to hand over to the Germans the credentials of those four
                            Delegations.</item>
                        <label>2.</label>
                        <item>—to place the aforesaid four Powers among the Powers to which the
                            Treaty is to be communicated before being delivered to the
                            Germans.</item>
                    </list></p>
            </div>
        </body>
